sec.p:
The cross-education of strength changes (1-RM strength, isokinetic peak torque at 20°·s−1 and 210°·s−1 and MVIC torque) were determined using a formula originally reported by Carroll and colleagues (Carroll et al. 2006). It calculates the difference between groups in the mean strength change in the weaker arm (i.e., non-trained arm in UNI) following the intervention period:\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym} 
				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
				\usepackage{amssymb} 
				\usepackage{amsbsy}
				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$$\left[ {\frac{{UNI_{post} {-} UNI_{pre} }}{{UNI_{pre} }} {-} \frac{{Detrain_{post} {-} Detrain_{pre} }}{{Detrain_{pre} }}} \right] \times 100,$$\end{document}UNIpost-UNIpreUNIpre-Detrainpost-DetrainpreDetrainpre×100,where UNIpre and UNIpost refer to mean strengths of the non-trained arm in UNI, and Detrainpre and Detrainpost refer to mean strengths of the weaker arm in Detrain, before and after the intervention period.
